cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "membrama"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Dmitrii O."
    family-names: "Chechetkin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/chedim/membrama"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  membrama is a GraphLink peer on llama.cpp that runs a local model for an AI seat
  and keeps the model's own attention cache (a KV bank) for an entity's text, loading
  it instead of reading the text again. It is a pure speed-up: the model sees the
  same tokens either way. The design records what was measured, including that a
  bank is safe only on its own in a prompt.
keywords:
  - llama.cpp
  - KV cache
  - GraphLink
  - local inference
  - memory
